---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'Noven — Get found when customers ask AI who to use';
const description =
  'Noven helps accountants, solicitors, clinics, consultancies and agencies get found and recommended when customers ask ChatGPT, Google, Copilot or Perplexity who to use. Start with a £30 audit.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>When your customers ask an AI who to use, the answer should include you.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        People increasingly ask ChatGPT, Google, Copilot and Perplexity to recommend an accountant,
        a solicitor, a clinic or a consultancy — instead of scrolling through search results. Noven
        does the work that gets your business into those answers.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Book the £30 audit</a>
        <a href="/how-it-works/">See how it works</a>
      </div>
      <p class="cta-note" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
        The audit is a written report on where you currently show up, and what's in the way. No
        obligation beyond the £30.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Why does this matter now?</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Buying habits have changed. Someone who needs a professional service used to type a
          query into Google and compare the results themselves. Now, many of them ask an AI
          assistant a direct question — <em>"Who's a good commercial solicitor near
          Manchester?"</em> — and get a short list of named businesses back.
        </p>
        <p>
          If your business isn't in that short list, you're not losing a ranking position. You're
          simply not part of the conversation, and you won't know it's happening, because there's
          no results page to check.
        </p>
        <p>
          The businesses that do appear are the ones whose information the AI systems can find,
          read and trust. That is fixable, and it's what Noven does.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tint">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>What does Noven actually do?</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Noven makes your business easy for AI assistants to find, understand and recommend. In
          practice that means three kinds of work:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 0.9rem;">
            <strong>We find out where you stand.</strong> We ask the major AI assistants the
            questions your customers ask, record what they say about you and your competitors, and
            trace why.
          </li>
          <li style="margin-bottom: 0.9rem;">
            <strong>We fix what's blocking you.</strong> Most businesses are invisible to these
            systems for mundane, correctable reasons: information the crawlers can't read,
            inconsistent facts across the web, or pages that never answer the questions customers
            actually ask.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>We keep you visible.</strong> The assistants and their sources change
            constantly. Ongoing plans keep your information current and extend your coverage to
            more of the questions that matter to you.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          It's methodical work, not a trick. There is no button we press that makes an AI
          recommend you — there is a set of things these systems demonstrably rely on, and we make
          sure you have them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Who is this for?</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Noven works with service businesses whose customers research and compare before buying:
          accountants, solicitors, private clinics, consultancies and agencies. If a client is
          worth hundreds or thousands of pounds to you, being one of the three names an AI
          suggests is worth taking seriously.
        </p>
        <p>
          It's a poor fit if your customers buy on impulse, or if you already have more work than
          you can take on.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-tint">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>Where's the proof?</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          An honest answer: Noven is a new business, and we don't yet have client case studies to
          show you. We won't invent any, and we'd encourage you to be suspicious of anyone in this
          field who shows you numbers that can't be checked.
        </p>
        <p>
          What we can show you is this website. It's built exactly the way we build for clients —
          plain, fast pages that assistants can read, structured information about the business,
          and a <a href="/faq/">real FAQ</a> that answers the questions people actually ask. Try
          it yourself: ask ChatGPT or Perplexity what Noven does and how much it costs, and see
          what comes back.
        </p>
        <p>
          [PLACEHOLDER: client case studies will be published here, with permission, as the first
          engagements complete.]
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <h2>What does it cost?</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          One service, priced in plain numbers. It starts with a <strong>£30 audit</strong> of
          where you currently show up. If there's work worth doing, the
          <strong>£350 Foundation</strong> setup gets you visible, and a monthly plan from
          <strong>£75</strong> keeps you that way. Full details, including what's in each part,
          are on the <a href="/pricing/">pricing page</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The audit is deliberately cheap so that finding out where you stand is an easy decision.
          If the audit shows you're already in good shape, we'll say so, and that's the end of it.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Book the £30 audit</a>
          <a href="/pricing/">See full pricing</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
